<title>INDIA: India ICRA awards &quot;1&quot; rating to Indo Mobil venture.</title>
<headline>India ICRA awards &quot;1&quot; rating to Indo Mobil venture.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Indo Mobil Ltd said on Friday the Investment Information and Credit Rating Agency (ICRA) has awarded its proposed LPG venture a &quot;1&quot; or &quot;good&quot; rating.  </p>
<p>Indo Mobil Ltd (IML) is a 50:50 joint venture between between state-run Indian Oil Corp and U.S.'s Mobil Corp .</p>
<p>IML will buy LPG at internationally competitive rates with assistance from IOC, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>It proposes to use the recently commissioned refrigerated LPG storage facilities of IOC at Kandla port in the western state of Gujarat and at other locations.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
